and the bronze helmet did not hold out, but right through
the bronze point broke the bone, and the brain
within, all of it, was spattered;

And again, from the scabbard having drawn his sharp sword,
Antiphates first, having rushed through the throng,
he struck at close quarters;

since it is not fitting at all, no, not at all,
for one who is of the people to speak out of line, neither in council
nor ever in war, but always to increase your strength;

So we, if indeed the gates and the wall of the Achaeans
we shall break with great strength, and the Achaeans give way,
not in order shall we come from the ships by the very same paths;
